{"kind":"request","text":"Make the documentation anchor gate refuse a retired anchor, or rename it to say what it checks.\n\nTestGateEveryNamedActResolvesToALiveRecord in internal/docset/anchor_test.go requires every act a page names to resolve to a real record whose kind is artifact. It does not ask whether that artifact has been retired. Five retired anchors across four pages passed it for as long as they existed, and the repair at e9a1c55a fixed the pages without touching the gate, so the same drift can happen again tomorrow.\n\nThe name is the part that misleads. \"ResolvesToALiveRecord\" reads as a liveness check, and live in this repository means not retired. The test's own comment is honest — it says it cannot settle whether the artifact is the right one for the prose — but a reader who trusts the name will believe anchors are checked for liveness when only existence and kind are checked.\n\nTwo ways to close it, and I do not think they are equally good.\n\nRefuse a retired anchor. This makes the gate mean what its name says, and it fails at the moment a supersession lands rather than whenever someone next happens to measure. The cost is coupling: retiring an artifact would redden the documentation gate until the pages that rest on it are re-anchored. That is arguably correct, because AGENTS.md already asks a merge to supersede and re-anchor together, but it makes one actor's supersession another actor's broken build, and that deserves a deliberate decision rather than my assumption.\n\nRename the test to say existence and kind. Cheap, honest, and leaves the defect undetected.\n\nI prefer refusing the retired anchor, but the coupling is a real cost and the person doing this should weigh it rather than inherit my preference. Whichever is chosen, the other should be ruled out in the report rather than left open.\n\nOne thing to check before implementing: whether any page legitimately rests on a retired artifact. I found none — the four I repaired were all defects — but the gate change asserts there can never be one, and that is a stronger claim than my measurement supports on its own.","body":{"conditions":"The anchor gate either refuses an anchor that resolves to a retired artifact, or is renamed so it no longer claims a liveness check it does not perform; the report states which was chosen and why the other was ruled out; the docset gates pass at the exact head; and if refusal is chosen, the report says what happens to the gate when an artifact is retired while a page still rests on it","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}